   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "זֶפֶת וְגׇפְרִית כְּדֵי לַעֲשׂוֹת כּוּ׳. תָּנָא: כְּדֵי לַעֲשׂוֹת נֶקֶב קָטָן.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: The measure that determines liability for carrying out «tar and sulfur» is equivalent to that which is used «to» seal a hole in a vessel and to «make a» small «hole» in that seal. Tar and sulfur were used to seal large cavities in jars. Holes were sometimes made in those seals. A tanna «taught» in a Tosefta: One is liable for carrying out a measure «equivalent» to that which can be used «to make» a large hole into «a small hole.»"
  }
